 "answer": "To configure LlamaIndex to use a local Ollama Large Language Model (LLM) and a Hugging Face embedding model globally, ensuring that OpenAI is never contacted, you can follow these steps based on the project's documentation context:\n\n1. **Install Necessary Packages:**\n   Ensure that you have the necessary packages installed, such as `llama-index`, `llama-index-embeddings-openai`, and any packages required for Ollama and Hugging Face embeddings.\n\n2. **Configure Global Settings:**\n   Use the `Settings` object to configure the global settings for LlamaIndex. This involves specifying the Ollama LLM and Hugging Face embedding models.\n\n3. **Set Up the Ollama LLM:**\n   Configure the `Settings` object to use Ollama as the LLM. This replaces any default or previously set LLMs, such as OpenAI.\n\n4. **Set Up Hugging Face Embeddings:**\n   Similarly, configure the `Settings` object to use a Hugging Face embedding model. This ensures that embeddings are generated locally without contacting external services.\n\nHere is a sample code snippet to achieve this configuration:\n\n```python\nfrom llama_index.llms.ollama import Ollama\nfrom llama_index.embeddings.huggingface import HuggingFaceEmbedding\nfrom llama_index.core import Settings\n\n# Set the Ollama LLM as the global LLM\nSettings.llm = Ollama()\n\n# Set the Hugging Face embedding model as the global embedding model\nSettings.embed_model = HuggingFaceEmbedding()\n\n# Example usage: creating a vector store index\nfrom llama_index.core import VectorStoreIndex, SimpleDirectoryReader\n\n# Load documents\ndocuments = SimpleDirectoryReader('path_to_your_documents').load_data()\n\n# Create a vector store index\nindex = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(documents)\n```\n\n### Additional Considerations:\n\n- **Local Runtime:** Ensure that Ollama and the Hugging Face embedding model are correctly set up and running on your local machine.\n- **Dependencies:** Install any additional dependencies required for Ollama and Hugging Face models.\n- **Documentation Links:** Refer to the documentation links provided in the context for more detailed examples and tutorials:\n  - [Local starter tutorial](/python/framework/getting_started/starter_example_local)\n  - [Using local LLMs](/python/framework/module_guides/models/llms/local)\n\nBy following these steps, you can configure LlamaIndex to operate entirely with local models, avoiding any external API calls to services like OpenAI.",
